      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I rarely have lag at all, even in big worlds. For me, lag almost always comes from loading a player's avatar, especially when there are more than 10 people or a large file size for someone's avatar. If you change the safety settings to only \"Voice\" and \"User Icons & Emoji's\" for every trust rank (visitor, new user, user, known user, trusted user, friends) this should stop almost all lag. After this, you can just show the avatars of the specific people you're talking to.\n\nI've used vrchat like this for many years, and I just click \"show avatar\" above the friend request button on every person I'm talking to and the game experience is the same as before, just safer and with no lag. You only need to click \"show avatar\" once, and will be able to see their avatar forever.\n\nIf it's the movement speed you're talking about, try using a keyboard or playstation controller to move instead of just your vive controllers. If the movement speed is still slow, it's likely just a weird setting for that world, like how some worlds don't allow you to jump or do certain things. If the movement is normal when pressing w, it's likely something with your vive trackpad, and you're not pressing high enough on the circle (it's slower when pressing the center as opposed to the top of the circle).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
